<title>CANADA: Spruce Falls Acquisition Q4 Sept 30 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Spruce Falls Acquisition Q4 Sept 30 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.43		   C$0.66</p>
<p> Net			 14,689		   22,693</p>
<p> Revs			82,952		   84,691</p>
<p>		  YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			 C$2.41		   C$1.49</p>
<p> Net			 83,124		   50,913</p>
<p> Revs		     347,242		  251,183</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Spruce Falls Acquisition Corp, which owns Spruce Falls Inc, an integrated newsprint and lumber making facility in Kapuskasing, Ontario. Spruce Falls Inc employees own 48 percent of the company's outstanding shares, while Tembec Inc owns 45 percent. The balance of shares are owned mainly by local residents.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Montreal bureau (514) 985-2434</p>
